# Database (node:sqlite)

Schema lives in `back-end/src/db/database.ts`, demo data in `back-end/src/db/seed.ts`, helpers in `back-end/src/db/sql.ts`.

## Queries

- Always use `?` placeholders. Never interpolate user input into SQL.
- Scope every employee-owned read by `employee_id`, and every support-staff read by `requests.team = staff team`. Before an update that uses only `id`, first confirm ownership or team:

```ts
// ✅ notifications.service.ts pattern
const owned = db.prepare("SELECT id FROM notifications WHERE id = ? AND employee_id = ?").get(id, employeeId);
if (!owned) throw new HttpError(404, "Bildirim bulunamadı.");
db.prepare("UPDATE notifications SET read = 1 WHERE id = ?").run(id);
```

- Wrap multi-statement writes in `transaction(db, () => ...)`, and read `lastInsertRowid` with `insertedId`.
- Store timestamps as ISO strings from the injected `now()`; never call `new Date()` inside a service.
- Map `snake_case` columns to `camelCase` response fields in the service, as `requestListItem` does.

## Data consistency

A request write must keep its related records in step in the same transaction:

- New request: `status = 'Yeni'`, a `Talep oluşturuldu` timeline row (`event_type` 'created', `visibility` 'public'), and a notification.
- New message: update `requests.updated_at`, and add the message and a public timeline row. A support message also adds an employee notification.
- Status change: update status and `updated_at`, add a public 'status_change' row with `from_status`/`to_status` labelled `Durum güncellendi: <status>`, and an employee notification (except the automatic change).
- Claim/assign/internal note: internal timeline rows only; internal notes live in `request_internal_notes`.
- Employees never change status directly; only `POST /api/support/requests/:id/status` and the automatic reply transition do.

## Schema changes

- `SCHEMA` in `database.ts` is the v0 baseline. Every later change is a numbered migration in `src/db/migrations.ts`, run in a transaction and recorded with `PRAGMA user_version`. Never edit an applied migration; add a new one.
- `CHECK` constraints repeat the status and priority lists from `src/config/constants.ts`. Change both together.
- `seedIfEmpty` runs only when `employees` is empty and writes v0-shaped data. Demo support staff are inserted by migration v1 (idempotent by email), so existing databases get them too. Keep seed data idempotent and clearly fictional (`ornek-kurum.com`), and keep at least 10 requests that cover every status.
